          %p i.e.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mi ℛ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{R}}
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\int_{B \in \mathcal{S}} \big(\mathcal{S}_{/B}\big)^{\ast/}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This follows readily from the definitions, but see also
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#BraunackMayer19"} Braunack-Mayer (2021), Rem. 1.15
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HebestreitSagaveSchlichtkrull20"} Hebestreit, Sagave &amp; Schlichtkrull (2020), Lem. 2.14
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retraction"} retraction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+homotopy+theory"} parameterized homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+spectrum"} parameterized spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+parameterized+spectra"} model structure for parameterized spectra
          %h2#references References
          %p The terminology “ex-spaces” is due to Ioan James, used for instance in:
          %ul
            %li#James95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"}> Ioan Mackenzie James
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+fibrewise+homotopy+theory"} Introduction to fibrewise homotopy theory
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"} Ioan Mackenzie James
              (ed.),
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
              (1995)
          %p
            Early discussion of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures includes
          %ul
            %li
              Michele Intermont,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Johnson"} Mark Johnson
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model structures on the category of ex-spaces
              %strong 119
              3 (2002) 325-353 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0166-8641(01)00076-1"}> doi:10.1016/S0166-8641(01)00076-1
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+for+parameterized+spectra"} model structures for parameterized spectra
          %ul
            %li#MaySigurdsson06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johann+Sigurdsson"} Johann Sigurdsson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Parametrized+Homotopy+Theory"} Parametrized Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-132"} ISBN:978-0-8218-3922-5
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0411656"} arXiv:math/0411656
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/EXTHEORY/MaySig.pdf"} pdf
            %li#BraunackMayer21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Braunack-Mayer"}> Vincent Braunack-Mayer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Combinatorial parametrised spectra
                %strong 21
                (2021) 801-891 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.08496"}> arXiv:1907.08496
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2021.21.801"} doi:10.2140/agt.2021.21.801
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (based on the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/thesis+Braunack-Mayer"} PhD thesis
            %li#HebestreitSagaveSchlichtkrull20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabian+Hebestreit"}> Fabian Hebestreit
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steffen+Sagave"} Steffen Sagave
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Schlichtkrull"} Christian Schlichtkrull
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Multiplicative parametrized homotopy theory via symmetric spectra in retractive spaces
                %strong 8
                (2020) e16 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.01824"}> arXiv:1904.01824
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/fms.2020.11"} doi:10.1017/fms.2020.11
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
                , Section 2.1 in:
                %em Parametrized spectra, a low-tech approach
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.04773"}> arXiv:1906.04773
                , user guide:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.math.binghamton.edu/malkiewich/users_guide_parametrized.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Malkiewich-ParametrizedSpectraUserGuide.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
